+## Isolated fixed-point core
+
+`DSFLOWER_DP_CORE_TESTING=ON` compiles a CPU-only test core and is off by
+default.  Test builds must explicitly provide the ABI-v2 deterministic
+`dsflower_dp_primitives` header and shared/import library.  This switch is not a
+capability switch and is never set by the production build script.
+
+The core clips and fixed-point quantizes one gradient/Hessian contribution per
+row, builds each active node histogram from its own rows, and sends the complete
+level vector through the exact discrete-Gaussian ABI before any split, missing
+direction, topology, leaf, gain, or cover is chosen.  The root total is included
+in the first joint release; later child totals are computed only from already
+privatized bins.  Binary logistic and bounded squared-error objectives use the
+same construction.  Raw histograms and the derived key are neither serialized
+nor copied into model configuration.
+
+ABI v3 also requires server-owned integer `fixed_point_scale`,
+`root_noise_scale`, and `level_noise_scale` values.  The core validates machine
+bounds but does not independently prove that they match the requested
+per-training privacy parameters, public geometry, and the
+`max_trees * max_depth` schedule.  The trusted adapter must calculate them with
+the checked reference accountant and bind them into the semantic key identity.
+
+Patient materialization, adapter calibration, interruption semantics, private
+evaluation exclusion, timing isolation, and model-egress sanitization remain
+release gates outside this core.  The process-local tree counter is defense in
+depth for one installed training context, not lifetime state.  A failed update
+reuses the same tree index and therefore the same PRF domain rather than
+creating a reroll.
